{
  "id": "vaccine-allocation-optimization-hea",
  "name": "Vaccine Allocation Optimization Model",
  "description": "Illustrative Vaccine Allocation Optimization Model. Source reconciliation 2026-10-20: The former DOI is Castillo et al.'s vaccine-market-design article; Bubar et al.'s correct DOI is now provided for conceptual context. This definition has fixed three-group allocation fractions and no epidemic/contact/serostatus dynamics, policy search or optimization objective; it is not Bubar's age-structured transmission model. Lives Saved multiplies doses by efficacy and IFR without infection-risk exposure or a counterfactual epidemic, so it is not an established estimate of deaths averted. All vaccination totals begin at zero, yielding 0/0 in Deaths per Million Vaccines. No ad hoc denominator guard or assumed infection risk was added. Scientific calibration and applicability remain unverified.",
  "stocks": [
